-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "881491ec-58d2-590b-b82a-17ce778f115d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151405} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c5ce70-0d54-55ec-8e04-3f4ed8c4debe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151406} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2d8a06-5188-58b3-a574-72be6221542c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151407} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9c22a4-be5d-51b9-973a-108340aac72e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151408} {:answer/id #uuid "7858a5f9-c6d7-5e62-8d5f-0b3f76c2d57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6c5ce70-0d54-55ec-8e04-3f4ed8c4debe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151406} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ae59f8c-bdfd-5e73-9a42-9cfdc24c36e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151404}] :question/id #uuid "5ba1b157-d35e-5ebb-b99d-e367dc0feceb" :question/math-academy-id "q-80438" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2616/Source/Images/q-80438.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If\n$f(x, y) = {\\frac{2x^{2}}{y},\\begin{vmatrix}(x, y) ∈ R∩D \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}(x, y) ∈ R∖D$,\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $∬_(D)\\frac{2x^{2}}{y}dA = ∬_(R)f(x, y)dA$, where $R = [0, 2] \\cdot [- 6, 6]$\n2. $∬_(R)\\frac{2x^{2}}{y}dA = ∬_(D)f(x, y)dA$, where $R = [- 1, 1] \\cdot [- 2, 2]$\n3. $∬_(D)\\frac{2x^{2}}{y}dA = ∬_(R)f(x, y)dA$, where $R = [- 2, 2] \\cdot [0, 4]$"}]}
